      "evidence": "The statement permits arbitrary T. With T=1, the tableau is 2x2, so there is no 2x3 window. The cited dependency lem-start-accept-and-transition-constraints-have-polynomial-size, step 1.2, says: “For each adjacent-row position and each illegal 2x3 pattern, add a clause forbidding that pattern.” Hence its move family is empty on this tableau. Let N reject epsilon in one step. The start and exactly-one constraints can be satisfied on row 0, and an accepting-state tag can be placed in row 1 to satisfy the accept disjunction; there is no transition clause preventing it. Thus psi_N,epsilon is satisfiable. But no accepting bounded computation tableau exists for N on epsilon, since def-bounded-computation-tableau requires every later row to be obtained by a legal transition and N rejects rather than accepts. The claimed biconditional is false.",
